# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Windows
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Office lock files. Excel writes ~$<name> beside an open workbook; it holds
# only the username of whoever has it open, and is left behind if Excel crashes.
~$*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Generated outputs (reproducible from data/ via src/ scripts). The rendered
# one-pagers land here and carry cohort counts derived from PHI.
**/output/

# Data files — keep patient/source data out of git (PHI-sensitive)
**/data/*.csv
**/data/**/*.csv
**/data/*.xlsx
**/data/**/*.xlsx
# ...except the analyte reference mapping, which carries no patient data.
!new_infogenerator/data/Analyte_Category_Mapping.xlsx
#
# data/validation_set.xlsx stays ignored, despite being a template. Its
# "example" sheet is a REAL cohort record, not synthetic: record 234 matches
# validate_v1.csv field for field — a 16-year-old, with collection date,
# facility, ethnicity, BAC, length of stay and full drug profile. Checked
# Sep 2026. Do not add an exception for it.

# Versioned data snapshots — versions live locally, out of git. They are derived
# and reproducible from data/ via src/, and the CSVs are PHI-sensitive.
new_infogenerator/versioned/*

# NOTE on what IS tracked, so it is not "tidied away" later:
#   new_infogenerator/README.md      the single reference for that directory
#   new_infogenerator/assets/        the state map the facility sheet embeds,
#                                    and the hand-drawn pipeline diagram.
#                                    Aggregate figures only, no patient data.
